  "model": "Sensitivity under a common EP16 retirement before downstream work, one dependency chain per phase, unchanged external gaps, fixed clocks and no transfer of eliminated work to another stage. Advancing the entire EP front by up to the largest pre-stage saving is credited, then the original last arrival to last exit is erased. Unchanged issuers and stage-relative gaps move with their prerequisites. Each local gather is charged its longest rank span, including waiting. The readout grants free native work through norm, excluding the invariant small logits projection. Scenarios which change upstream readiness, remove host launch gaps or let individual ranks use partial results before the common join need their own wider schedule model.",
  "interpretation": "Fixed clocks, arrivals/joins as in the source, same four service carriers. Scope means these measured terms may change, full saving is free. A subset of a failing scope inherits the screen. Passing the guide establishes budget only. A changed join, earlier consumer, different frequency or wider producer region requires a different model.",
